    response: `<strong>Combat Tactics and Psychology of Yangyiquan:</strong>

<strong>The Fundamental War Paradox</strong>
<em>"Have the intention of defending yourself when you attack — that will give you victory."</em> A warrior fighting with defensive intent generates fluid, explosive, precise movements. One fighting from anger or arrogance generates tense, telegraphed, premature strikes. Intent modifies biomechanical quality at the muscular level.

<strong>Prior Knowledge — Victory Before Combat</strong>
The real battle occurs before the first strike. Define targets. Identify adversary deficiencies. Choose attack sequences. <em>"Tell yourself: Now I attack — and then attack. Inner certainty creates a disturbance in the adversary's perception field that prevents effective reaction."</em>

<strong>Annihilation Strategy — Destroy the Foundation</strong>
<em>"The knees are the pillars of the adversary's house."</em> Attack what is slow. Destroy the structural base. <em>"Do not allow the adversary to root their confidence. Make them dance like a foolish dancer."</em> A combatant without leg mobility has lost capacity to generate power, move, or maintain balance under pressure.

<strong>Tactical Blindness — Temporary Vision Compromise</strong>
Threaten the eyes with fingers — not as an end, but as distraction forcing the adversary to elevate their guard and expose lower flanks. The real attack follows immediately. <em>"If God were blind, who would rule the earth?"</em>`
